# ── SEC25-D-04 (2026-08-25 security audit, area D) ────────────────────────
# Agent scratch: probes, censuses and one-off queries live as ROOT-LEVEL
# DOTFILES in the working checkout (~50 of them observed: .aran-probe*.mjs,
# .census-*.mjs, .vadverify-*.mjs, .q1.mjs, .fontprobe*.mjs, and their .json /
# .md outputs). Several read SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from disk at runtime and
# their outputs carry live learner data. Nothing ignored them, so a single
# `git add -A` / `git add .` in the main checkout would have staged the lot.
# Ignore the whole root-dotfile class and re-admit, by name, the ones that are
# genuinely part of the repo.
/.*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.github/
# .claude/ is ignored wholesale further up; settings.json is tracked deliberately.
!/.claude/
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.npmrc
!/.nvmrc
!/.editorconfig
!/.prettierrc
!/.prettierrc.*
!/.eslintrc
!/.eslintrc.*
!/.eslintignore
!/.node-version
!/.vercelignore

# Local databases and their journals — the command surface keeps
# `command-surface.db` at the repo root, and it is not repo content.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Belt-and-braces on the secret class: any .env variant, anywhere, and the
# key/cert file types. `.env` and `.env.local` were already covered; these
# catch `.env.production`, `api/.env`, stray `*.pem` and `*.key`.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
